1. DEFINITIONS

1.1  "Personal Use" means use by an individual for their own private purposes,
     including hobby projects, personal photos and video, learning, coursework
     and unpaid personal creative work.

1.2  "Commercial Use" means any use in, for, or on behalf of a business,
     organisation or professional practice. It includes, without limitation:
     use inside a company even where nothing is sold; freelance or client work
     you invoice for; producing material for a paid product, service or
     subscription; and any use with an anticipated commercial application.

1.3  "Charitable and Academic Use" means use by a registered charity, school,
     college, university, public research body, public health or safety
     organisation, or government body, for its own non-revenue purposes.
     Charitable and Academic Use is treated as Personal Use under this
     agreement, regardless of how the organisation is funded, and is not
     Commercial Use.

1.4  "Video Input Volume" means the cumulative total file size of all video
     files you submit to the Software for processing, measured across all time
     and all devices, and counted once per file processed.

1.5  "Still Images" means single-frame image files. Still Images do not count
     toward Video Input Volume.

1.6  "Image Count" means the cumulative total number of Still Images you submit
     to the Software for processing, measured across all time and all devices,
     and counted once per image processed.

1.7  "Third-Party Components" means the software and neural-network model
     weights authored by others and distributed with, or downloaded by, the
     Software. These are listed in NOTICE.md.


2. THE FREE TIER

2.1  We grant you a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive,
     non-transferable licence to install and run the Software for Personal Use,
     at no charge, within both of the following allowances:

     (a) a Video Input Volume of up to 1 gigabyte (1 GB, being 1,073,741,824
         bytes); and
     (b) an Image Count of up to 100 Still Images.

2.2  The two allowances are independent. Exceeding one does not consume the
     other: you may reach 100 images while still having video allowance left,
     and the reverse.

2.3  Once you exceed either allowance, continued processing of that kind
     requires a Personal Licence under clause 3 or a Commercial Licence under
     clause 4. Your existing outputs remain yours and are unaffected, and you
     may continue to use the Software within any allowance you have not yet
     exhausted.

2.4  The Free Tier does not permit Commercial Use in any volume. Commercial Use
     requires a Commercial Licence from the first byte.


3. PERSONAL LICENCE — Rs 513 + GST IN INDIA, US$10 ELSEWHERE, ONE-TIME

3.1  On payment of a one-time fee of Rs 513 plus GST (if you are in India) or US$10
     (elsewhere) we grant you a perpetual, worldwide,
     royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to install and run
     the Software for Personal Use with no limit on Video Input Volume and no
     limit on Image Count. A single Personal Licence removes both allowances;
     there is no separate charge for images and video.

3.2  A Personal Licence is granted to one named individual. That individual may
     install and run the Software on any number of devices that they own or
     personally control. The licence follows the person, not the machine.

3.3  A Personal Licence is perpetual for the version series it is purchased
     under and all later releases we make available under these terms. It does
     not expire, is not a subscription, and requires no renewal.

3.4  A Personal Licence does not permit Commercial Use.


4. COMMERCIAL LICENCE — Rs 8,228 + GST IN INDIA, US$200 ELSEWHERE, ONE-TIME

4.1  On payment of a one-time fee of Rs 8,228 plus GST (if your organisation
     is established in India) or US$200 (elsewhere) we grant you a perpetual,
     worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to
     install and run the Software for Commercial Use with no limit on Video
     Input Volume and no limit on Image Count. As with clause 3.1, a single
     Commercial Licence removes both allowances.

4.2  A Commercial Licence is granted to one legal entity and covers that
     entity's employees and contractors acting on its behalf, on any number of
     devices, for that entity's own work. It does not extend to a parent,
     subsidiary or affiliated company, each of which requires its own licence.

4.3  A Commercial Licence is perpetual on the same basis as clause 3.3.

4.4  A Commercial Licence covers using the Software to produce work. It does
     not permit redistributing, reselling, sublicensing or hosting the Software
     itself as a product or service to third parties. For that, contact us.


4A. REGIONAL PRICING, TAX AND CURRENCY

4A.1 PGA Tech Solutions is a sole proprietorship established in India
     (Uttar Pradesh, GSTIN 09AIAPG7383C1ZE). Prices in rupees are for
     buyers in India; prices in US dollars are for buyers elsewhere. Which
     applies is determined by where you, or the organisation taking the
     licence, are established - not by the payment method you happen to use.

4A.2 Indian sales are made by PGA Tech Solutions directly. PGA Tech Solutions
     is registered for GST in India (GSTIN: 09AIAPG7383C1ZE). Prices shown in
     rupees are exclusive of GST. GST at the applicable rate, currently 18% on
     software licences (SAC 997331), is added at checkout, and the amount
     payable including GST is shown before you pay. A tax invoice showing the
     GST charged is issued for every Indian sale.

4A.3 Sales outside India may be made through a third-party reseller acting as
     merchant of record. Where that is so, the reseller is the seller for tax
     purposes, collects any VAT, GST or sales tax due in your country, and
     appears on your statement. The licence you receive is still granted by
     PGA Tech Solutions on these terms.

4A.4 Supplies to buyers outside India are exports of service and are
     zero-rated under Indian GST, supplied under Letter of Undertaking without
     payment of IGST.

4A.5 All prices are exclusive of tax. Indian GST is added at checkout by us;
     tax outside India is added at checkout by the merchant of record. No
     separate charge is made for payment processing: the price is the price,
     plus tax. We may change prices for future purchases; a licence already
     granted is not affected.


